---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import { locations, navItems } from "../../data/site";
---

<Layout
	title="Your Guide is on its Way · Awaken Discovery"
	description="Your free teacher's guide is on its way — open your inbox to begin."
>
	<SiteHeader navItems={navItems} />
	<main class="ty-page">
		<!-- ============== CONFIRMATION ============== -->
		<section class="ty-hero">
			<div class="container ty-hero-inner">
				<p class="ty-eyebrow">Thank you</p>
				<h1>Your Guide is on its Way…</h1>
				<p class="ty-lede">
					Check your email in the next few minutes for <em>Why You Can't Switch Off After Teaching — A Teacher's Guide to Grounding Yourself
					When You're Already Overwhelmed.</em>
				</p>
				<p class="ty-aside">
					(If you don't see it, check your spam folder. The last thing you need is
					another thing going missing.)
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ============== HONEST PIVOT ============== -->
		<section class="ty-band">
			<div class="container ty-prose">
				<h2>But Before You Go Back to Marking…</h2>
				<p>Can I be brutally honest with you for a second?</p>
				<p>
					That guide you just downloaded? It's going to help you get through the next
					few weeks.
				</p>
				<p>It really is.</p>
				<p>
					But here's what I've noticed after working with dozens of teachers
					struggling with anxiety and burnout:
				</p>
				<p class="ty-emphasis">
					The ones who actually <em>change</em> their situation — the ones who
					aren't still drowning six months from now — they do one thing differently.
				</p>
				<blockquote class="ty-quote">
					They start noticing the patterns <em>before</em> they hit crisis point.
				</blockquote>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ============== PATTERN ============== -->
		<section class="ty-band ty-band-soft">
			<div class="container ty-prose">
				<h2>Because Here's What Happens to Most Teachers</h2>
				<p>
					You push through September. You survive October. You white-knuckle your way
					to half-term.
				</p>
				<p>
					Then you collapse for a week, feel slightly better, and go back in thinking
					"this term will be different."
				</p>
				<p class="ty-emphasis">But it never is.</p>
				<p>Because you never stopped to notice what's actually triggering your anxiety.</p>
				<ul class="ty-questions">
					<li>Is it certain classes? Certain times of day? Certain types of meetings or interactions?</li>
					<li>Is it the workload? The behaviour management? The constant feeling that you're being judged?</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="ty-pull">You can't fix what you can't see.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ============== JOURNAL OFFER ============== -->
		<section class="ty-offer">
			<div class="container ty-offer-grid">
				<figure class="ty-offer-mockup">
					<img
						src="/assets/images/teachers-guide-journal.svg"
						alt="Soft illustration of the upcoming Teachers Reflection Journal"
						loading="lazy"
						decoding="async"
					/>
				</figure>
				<div class="ty-offer-copy">
					<p class="ty-eyebrow">For teachers who download the guide</p>
					<h2>Teachers Reflection Journal</h2>
					<p>
						This isn't some generic journal with blank pages and vague prompts about
						gratitude. This is specifically designed for teachers who are trying to
						survive an impossible job without losing themselves completely.
					</p>
					<p>Inside the journal, you'll get:</p>
					<ul class="ty-inside">
						<li>
							<strong>Weekly reflection prompts</strong> that help you spot your
							anxiety triggers <em>before</em> you hit burnout — so you can actually
							do something about them.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Space to track what's happening in your body, thoughts and
							emotions</strong> across the school week (because Tuesday anxiety hits
							different than Friday anxiety).
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Tools to build your own personalised "survival toolkit"</strong> for the situations that drain you most.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>Guided exercises</strong> to help you process the guilt, the
							frustration, and the constant feeling that you're not doing enough.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong>A structured way to figure out if you can make teaching
							sustainable</strong> — or if it's time to plan your exit strategy.
						</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ============== HONESTY ============== -->
		<section class="ty-band">
			<div class="container ty-prose">
				<h2>Because Here's the Thing Nobody Tells You</h2>
				<p>Sometimes the answer isn't "better self-care."</p>
				<p class="ty-emphasis">
					Sometimes the answer is "this job is incompatible with my mental health."
				</p>
				<p>And that's okay.</p>
				<p>
					But you need to make that decision from a place of <em>clarity</em>… not
					from a place of crisis.
				</p>
				<p>The journal helps you get that clarity.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ============== COMING SOON ============== -->
		<section class="ty-discount">
			<div class="container ty-discount-inner">
				<p class="ty-eyebrow">Coming soon</p>
				<h2>The Journal Is Still Being Shaped</h2>
				<p>
					The Teachers Reflection Journal isn't ready just yet —
					I'm taking my time to make sure it genuinely helps teachers like
					you, rather than rushing something out before it's right.
				</p>
				<p>
					Because you've just joined the free guide list, you'll be the
					first to hear when it's available — and the first to be offered
					an early reader discount.
				</p>
				<p class="ty-emphasis">
					In the meantime, the free guide you've just downloaded is a
					complete tool on its own. Start there.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- ============== SOFT CLOSE ============== -->
		<section class="ty-band ty-band-soft">
			<div class="container ty-prose">
				<p>Or, if you're not ready yet, that's okay too.</p>
				<p>You've got the free guide. Start there.</p>
				<p>I'll be in your inbox soon with more support specifically for teachers.</p>
				<p class="ty-emphasis">Take care of yourself. (I mean it.)</p>
				<p class="ty-signoff">— Ally</p>

				<aside class="ty-ps">
					<p>
						<strong>P.S.</strong> Keep an eye on your inbox over the coming
						weeks. I'll be sharing more support specifically for teachers —
						and the moment the Teachers Reflection Journal is
						ready, you'll be among the first to know.
					</p>
				</aside>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
	<SiteFooter
		locations={locations}
		tagline="Helping overwhelmed teachers reconnect with themselves beyond survival mode."
	/>
</Layout>

<style>
	.ty-page {
		--ink: var(--color-dark-gray);
		--brand: var(--color-dark-slate-gray);
		--brand-deep: #004836;
		--cream: #fbf9f5;
		--cream-deep: #f3eee5;
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.75;
		color: var(--ink);
		background: var(--cream);
	}

	.ty-page :global(.cta) {
		font-size: 1rem;
		padding: 0.9rem 1.4rem;
	}

	.ty-hero {
		padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vh, 6rem);
		background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--cream) 0%, var(--cream-deep) 100%);
	}

	.ty-hero-inner {
		max-width: 60ch;
	}

	.ty-eyebrow {
		margin: 0;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--brand);
	}

	.ty-hero h1 {
		margin: 0.55rem 0 0.9rem;
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.4vw, 3.1rem);
		font-weight: 500;
		line-height: 1.16;
	}

	.ty-lede {
		margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
	}

	.ty-aside {
		margin: 0;
		font-style: italic;
		opacity: 0.75;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
	}

	.ty-band {
		padding-block: clamp(2.4rem, 6vh, 4rem);
	}

	.ty-band-soft {
		background: var(--cream-deep);
	}

	.ty-prose {
		max-width: 64ch;
	}

	.ty-prose h2 {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.8vw, 2rem);
		font-weight: 500;
		line-height: 1.22;
	}

	.ty-prose p {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}

	.ty-emphasis {
		font-weight: 500;
		font-size: 1.08rem;
	}

	.ty-pull {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-style: italic;
		font-size: 1.35rem;
		color: var(--brand);
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
	}

	.ty-quote {
		margin: 1.2rem 0;
		padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem;
		border-left: 3px solid var(--brand);
		background: rgb(0 94 71 / 6%);
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-style: italic;
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		color: var(--brand-deep);
		border-radius: 0 0.6rem 0.6rem 0;
	}

	.ty-questions {
		margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
		padding-left: 1.2rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.5rem;
	}

	/* OFFER */
	.ty-offer {
		padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vh, 5rem);
		background: linear-gradient(160deg, #eaf0ea 0%, var(--cream-deep) 100%);
	}

	.ty-offer-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 0.85fr 1.15fr;
		gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem);
		align-items: center;
	}

	.ty-offer-mockup img {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 360px;
		margin-inline: auto;
		filter: drop-shadow(0 18px 36px rgb(0 94 71 / 18%));
	}

	.ty-offer-copy h2 {
		margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.3vw, 2.3rem);
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.ty-inside {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.85rem;
	}

	.ty-inside li {
		position: relative;
		padding-left: 2rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
	}

	.ty-inside li::before {
		content: "✓";
		position: absolute;
		left: 0;
		top: 0;
		width: 1.4rem;
		height: 1.4rem;
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: var(--brand);
		color: var(--color-white);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	/* DISCOUNT */
	.ty-discount {
		padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vh, 5rem);
		background: var(--cream);
	}

	.ty-discount-inner {
		max-width: 64ch;
	}

	.ty-discount h2 {
		margin: 0.5rem 0 0.8rem;
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 2.4rem);
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.ty-discount > .ty-discount-inner > p,
	.ty-discount > .ty-discount-inner > h2 {
		max-width: 60ch;
	}

	.ty-signoff {
		font-family: var(--font-script);
		font-size: 2rem;
		color: var(--brand);
		margin: 1rem 0;
	}

	.ty-ps {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem;
		background: var(--color-white);
		border-left: 3px solid var(--brand);
		border-radius: 0 0.85rem 0.85rem 0;
	}

	.ty-ps p {
		margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 1024px) {
		.ty-offer-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
